AGRIMARKET
PRACTICAL ASSESSMENT 2
TESTING AND DEBUGGING REPORT
Project: AgriMarket Online Produce Marketplace
Technology: PHP 8, MySQL/MariaDB, HTML, CSS, JavaScript, Tailwind CSS
Assessment basis: Static review of the supplied agrimarket-main source archive
IMPORTANT NOTE ON TEST EVIDENCE
This report follows the structure and style of the example report supplied. It is based on inspection of the actual AgriMarket project. All 29 PHP files in the archive were checked with the PHP 8.4.24 command-line syntax checker and reported no syntax errors. However, this was a static syntax check, not a full application execution or browser test.
The supplied archive has important integration problems: the includes/ directory referenced by several pages is missing, and different parts of the code use incompatible database/configuration conventions. Therefore, end-to-end functional, security, payment and browser test results cannot honestly be reported as passed. Test cases below are proposed execution cases unless specifically marked as a completed static check.
TASK 1: SUMMARY OF TESTING AND TYPES OF TESTING
1.1 Introduction
Testing is required to establish whether AgriMarket behaves according to its requirements, handles invalid information safely and protects buyer, farmer and administrator information. The project contains pages and API endpoints for registration, login, produce browsing, cart management, checkout, receipts, profiles, farmer pages and administration.
The first review focused on understanding the source files, database schema, configuration and dependencies. A PHP syntax check was then carried out on every PHP file in the archive. All 29 files passed this syntax check. Runtime testing is blocked until the missing shared include files and conflicting application/database structures are reconciled.
1.2 Types of Testing Required
Testing type	Areas to test	Purpose
Static code / syntax testing	All PHP files, includes and configuration	Identify syntax errors and unresolved dependencies before execution.
Functional testing	Registration, login, catalogue, product details, cart, checkout, orders and receipts	Confirm that each feature performs its intended task.
Validation and negative testing	Email, phone, password, quantities, stock, prices, delivery details and uploads	Confirm invalid or out-of-range data is rejected.
Database testing	Users, categories, products, orders and order_items	Check schema compatibility, relationships, constraints and data persistence.
Security testing	Authentication, role checks, CSRF, SQL injection, XSS, sessions, uploads and payment callback	Protect accounts, records and payment processes.
Usability and compatibility	Navigation, forms, responsive layout and JavaScript interactions	Check that the application is usable on common devices and browsers.
Payment integration testing	M-Pesa simulation, Daraja request and callback handling	Verify payment status handling without treating simulation as a real payment.
Regression testing	All corrected modules	Ensure fixes do not break other features.

