TASK 4: SECURITY TESTING
4.1 Introduction
Security testing should establish whether the application protects personal data, account credentials, order records, uploaded images and payment information. The source contains prepared security-related mechanisms such as PDO prepared statements, password hashing in the seed script, CSRF helper patterns in functions.php, role checks in some pages and a simulated M-Pesa mode. These mechanisms still require runtime verification and consistent integration.
