TASK 6: DEFECT REPORT
6.1 Introduction
A defect is a fault in the application that can cause incorrect behaviour, prevent a feature from running or expose the system to risk. The following issues were identified by inspecting the supplied source archive. They should be logged and retested after correction.
6.2 Defects and Integration Issues Identified
ID	Affected area	Observed issue	Impact / severity
D-01	Application bootstrap	index.php, register.php and other pages require files under includes/, but no includes/ directory is present in the supplied ZIP.	Critical – key pages cannot bootstrap.
D-02	Authentication integration	Several files call includes/auth_middleware.php and functions such as require_login(), verify_csrf() and csrf_field(), while the archive does not contain that middleware file.	Critical – authentication-dependent pages cannot run as supplied.
D-03	Database model mismatch	database/schema.sql defines users.id, first_name, last_name and products; root functions.php and other pages contain queries referencing user_id, full_name, status, location, produce and other fields/tables not defined in the supplied schema.	Critical – SQL queries may fail at runtime.
D-04	Configuration duplication	config.php and config/constants.php define overlapping constants and use different connection/configuration paths.	High – duplicate definitions or inconsistent runtime settings.
D-05	Database helper duplication	config/db.php defines db() separately from the connection function in functions.php.	High – risk of conflicting database helper definitions.
D-06	Administrator route naming	The archive contains admin/darshboard.php (misspelled) while links in other files refer to admin/dashboard.php.	Medium – administrator navigation may lead to a missing page.
D-07	Farmer/profile query compatibility	farmer_profile.php queries fields such as user_id, full_name, location, bio and status that are absent from the supplied users table definition.	High – farmer profile query is incompatible with schema.
D-08	Missing assets	The visible archive listing does not include an assets/images directory although page templates reference image assets there.	Low/Medium – images may be missing when rendered.

6.3 Classification
Defect class	Examples	Recommended action
Missing dependency	D-01, D-02	Restore the intended shared include files or refactor all pages to use the included root-level helpers.
Database/schema mismatch	D-03, D-07	Choose one schema and update all SQL queries and seed data to match it.
Configuration/integration	D-04, D-05	Keep one configuration loader and one PDO connection function.
Routing/file naming	D-06	Rename the dashboard file or update all links consistently.
Presentation asset gap	D-08	Include required image files or replace references with available assets.

